    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p4-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "If $\\log_2 a=3$ and $\\log_2 b=4$, then find $\\log_2 ab$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$7$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a&=2^3,\\qquad b=2^4\\\\ab&=2^3\\times2^4\\\\ab&=2^7\\\\\\log_2 ab&=7\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If $\\log_3 a=5$ and $\\log_3 b=6$, then find $\\log_3 ab$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$11$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a&=3^5,\\qquad b=3^6\\\\ab&=3^5\\times3^6\\\\ab&=3^{11}\\\\\\log_3 ab&=11\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What do you notice about the previous two questions? Can you make and prove a conjecture?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p4-q7-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The logarithm of a product is the sum of the logarithms: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\log_b(xy)=\\log_b x+\\log_b y",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", for positive x and y and a positive base b other than 1.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p4-q7-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Write the factors as powers of the same base and add their indices.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "In both cases, the logarithm of the product equals the sum of the given logarithms.\n\nConjecture: $\\log_b(xy)=\\log_b x+\\log_b y$, where $x,y>0$, $b>0$ and $b\\ne1$.\n\nLet $m=\\log_b x$ and $n=\\log_b y$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=b^m,\\qquad y=b^n\\\\xy&=b^m b^n\\\\xy&=b^{m+n}\\\\\\log_b(xy)&=m+n\\\\\\log_b(xy)&=\\log_b x+\\log_b y.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
